// APNT created-note seal v0 — the complete locking bytecode.
//
// Maturity: stable — compiled by apnt_created_note_seal_v0.ts; not yet
// exercised by any published verify:* command. See AGENTS.md, "The maturity
// ladder".
//
// Target architecture:
// openspec/changes/define-apnt-private-spend-covenant-v0/design.md §3.1,
// with the branch decisions in §1.1.6a (witness-index aggregate branch) and
// §1.2 (direct-exit branch).
//
// This is what a created note's output is actually locked by. It is a BARE
// DIRECT-P2S locking script, not a P2SH32 wrapper, and that is load-bearing:
// both branches are therefore visible on-chain at note-creation time, so any
// observer can read a created seal's output script and confirm that an exit
// branch exists and which key it commits to. Behind a P2SH32 hash the branches
// would stay hidden until spend time and the mandatory-exit property would only
// be checkable in-circuit (design.md §3.1).
//
// Measured composition, against maximumStandardLockingBytecodeLength = 201:
//
//     OP_IF   (1) + aggregate branch (74) + OP_ELSE (1)
//                 + exit branch      (51) + OP_ENDIF (1)   = 128 bytes
//
// design.md §3.1 originally recorded 130 bytes. That figure summed §1.1.6's
// last-input aggregate branch (76 bytes); §1.1.6a adopted the witness-index
// variant (74 bytes) instead, so the real seal is 128. Both figures fit the
// same 201-byte limit.
//
// Branch selection is the top unlocking-bytecode stack item, so a spender's
// witness ends with the selector:
//
//     aggregate spend   push(designatedVerifierInputIndex) OP_1
//     exit spend        push(signature65) push(exitPublicKey33) OP_0
//
// Both selectors are minimal encodings (OP_1 pushes 0x01, OP_0 pushes the empty
// item), which is what the VM's minimal-`OP_IF` rule requires.
//
// BOTH BRANCHES ARE SIMULTANEOUSLY LIVE for the whole lifetime of a seal. A
// recipient can broadcast an exit while an aggregate settlement for the same
// seal is in flight; whichever confirms first wins and the other becomes invalid
// because it spends a consumed outpoint. That is a liveness consideration for
// aggregators, not a fund-security one (design.md §3.3).
//
// TRAP, recorded because it is easy to get wrong and expensive to discover late:
// OP_CHECKSIG's covered bytecode is the ENTIRE locking script it executes under
// — this whole 128-byte seal — not the 51-byte exit branch in isolation. A
// signature produced against the bare branch does NOT validate here. The
// reference-aggregator seal-level verification module executes exactly that
// rejection so the trap is a measurement rather than a comment.
//
// SCOPE. This template is the WALLET-SIDE half of design.md §3.2's two
// enforcement levels: it makes the exit branch visible on-chain at creation
// time.
//
// CORRECTED 2026-08-13. This comment previously said the second level — an
// accepted transition recomputing this template and requiring byte equality
// with the created output's locking bytecode — was "deliberately NOT
// implemented anywhere in this repository". That is no longer true, and the
// stale text directly contradicted `apnt_created_note_seal_v0.ts`, which says
// "Both levels now exist". Both files are published, so a reader saw the
// contradiction and could not resolve it.
//
// Both levels now exist. The second lives in
// `apnt_created_note_seal_skeleton_v0.ts` as a fixed-offset byte matcher over a
// pinned skeleton (a guest must not read files or run the CASM compiler), and
// is applied by the v1 structural validator and the transition relation, and by
// import relations V3/V4 for import-created outputs.
//
// Note the scope word that made the old text wrong: "anywhere in this
// repository" is a bare universal with no named subject. The accurate scoped
// statement would have been "not implemented in the transition relation at the
// time of writing".
//
// This is a locking-template artifact. It is not APNT acceptance, proof
// verification, chain validation, wallet acceptance, or note spendability.

OP_IF

// --- aggregate branch: delegate to the settlement authorization covenant ----
@AGGREGATE_BRANCH_SOURCE@

OP_ELSE

// --- direct-exit branch: the non-custodial floor, one on-chain signature ----
@EXIT_BRANCH_SOURCE@

OP_ENDIF
